From 1ba258f903c6c309e60a792950dd29f96a671db9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miller Bath <millerzbath@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:40:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: send a folder with hc put, and --progress lines
 while sending

hc put sends a folder file by file into one new folder there (name-2,
... when taken), each file in its place; links are not followed. The
core takes folder (and fresh, for the new folder) on terminal.put.

--progress prints one JSON line on stderr per piece: bytes sent of the
whole file or folder, and the file it is on, for an app to show.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
